plank (0.13~dev-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix the dock crawling away from its edge on desktops that are not GNOME or
    Unity.  There, monitor_geo is the work area, and the work area already
    contains the strut we asked for, so placement was computed from a value
    placement itself had changed: every refresh moved the dock one more
    dock-thick towards the screen centre and grew the strut by the same amount.
    PositionManager now remembers which edge the last strut went to and how
    much of it was ours, and adds that space back when reading the work area,
    which makes the bottom dock land on the bottom and stay there.

 -- NextToMinus <nexttominus@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:24:53 +0800

plank (0.12-2) noble; urgency=medium

  * One binary package again: the dock, the shared library, the docklets, the
    themes and the translations all ship inside plank.  The previous split
    meant "apt install ./plank_0.12-1_amd64.deb" failed on its own siblings
    (apt cannot fetch libplank1/libplank-common out of a plain directory),
    nothing links against libplank out of tree, and an Architecture:all data
    package saves nothing when only amd64 is ever built.  Breaks/Replaces evict
    the old libplank1, libplank-common and plank-docklets in one transaction.
  * Development files (headers, pkg-config file, Vala bindings, the unversioned
    .so symlink) are no longer distributed at all; see debian/not-installed.

 -- NextToMinus <nexttominus@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:18:13 +0800

plank (0.12-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fork release 0.12: null-pointer fixes in ApplicationDockItem, hardened
    Applications menu provider, warning before a pinned launcher file is
    dropped, and a build timestamp in the about dialog.
  * Packaging: split plank / libplank1 / plank-docklets / libplank-common /
    libplank-dev, install into the multiarch libdir, depend on bamfdaemon so
    running applications show up out of the box.

 -- NextToMinus <nexttominus@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:16:57 +0800
